WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.292 --> 00:00:20.613
horrible!" Ben hung his head as he sat at the kitchen table.

2
00:00:20.633 --> 00:00:25.254
"Winnie's costumes are ruined, and the black cauldron is bright blue!

3
00:00:25.274 --> 00:00:27.815
I ruined the show!"

4
00:00:27.835 --> 00:00:31.296
"I doubt that," Uncle Bert said.

5
00:00:31.904 --> 00:00:32.524
"It's true!

6
00:00:32.884 --> 00:00:35.065
Everyone was worried about the curse of Macdeath.

7
00:00:35.725 --> 00:00:36.785
Well, guess what?

8
00:00:37.426 --> 00:00:38.786
I'm the curse of Macdeath."

9
00:00:40.046 --> 00:00:41.327
Uncle Bert shook his head.

10
00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:43.507
"We talked about this, Ben.

11
00:00:44.007 --> 00:00:46.008
Superstitions aren't real.

12
00:00:46.368 --> 00:00:49.629
They're made-up stories, just like Quakespeare's plays.

13
00:00:50.109 --> 00:00:53.550
Most monsters, even actors, don't take them seriously."

14
00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:59.612
"If there's no curse," Ben said, "how do you explain all the weird things that have happened?"

15
00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.442
"Accidents," Uncle Bert replied.

16
00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:05.964
"You should go easier on yourself."

17
00:01:05.984 --> 00:01:07.846
"I can't!"

18
00:01:08.246 --> 00:01:08.886
Ben said.

19
00:01:08.907 --> 00:01:11.489
"Everyone is going to hate me forever."

20
00:01:11.509 --> 00:01:15.172
"No, they won't," Uncle Bert said.

21
00:01:15.192 --> 00:01:17.514
"A show's cast is like a family.

22
00:01:18.274 --> 00:01:19.775
And everyone makes mistakes.

23
00:01:20.216 --> 00:01:23.599
You can't let those mistakes stop you from doing something you like.

24
00:01:24.039 --> 00:01:25.760
Or getting to know someone you like."

25
00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:29.083
"You mean like your crush?"

26
00:01:29.403 --> 00:01:30.024
Ben asked.

27
00:01:31.056 --> 00:01:32.077
Uncle Bert nodded.

28
00:01:32.097 --> 00:01:36.899
"I regret letting my nerves get the better of me during my school play.

29
00:01:37.499 --> 00:01:38.719
You have a choice.

30
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:42.201
You can run away and hide, like I did.

31
00:01:42.841 --> 00:01:44.622
Or you can fix what's broken.

32
00:01:45.702 --> 00:01:50.004
Besides, you have a responsibility to make sure the show goes on."

33
00:01:52.185 --> 00:01:54.326
Ben sighed, thinking for a moment.

34
00:01:54.886 --> 00:01:58.868
He didn't really want to quit—he liked acting and being part of the cast.

35
00:02:00.148 --> 00:02:05.032
Victoria had even complimented him several times, telling him he was a talented actor.

36
00:02:05.052 --> 00:02:08.955
"Dad has some black paint in the garage.

37
00:02:09.415 --> 00:02:11.197
I guess I could repaint the cauldron."

38
00:02:12.338 --> 00:02:13.318
Ben shook his head.

39
00:02:13.339 --> 00:02:15.620
"But what about the costumes?"

40
00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:18.302
"You'll have to find replacements."

41
00:02:18.322 --> 00:02:21.165
"That will be hard," Ben said.

42
00:02:21.185 --> 00:02:22.286
"Can you help me?"

43
00:02:22.306 --> 00:02:25.168
"I thought you'd never ask!"

44
00:02:30.492 --> 00:02:35.113
After dropping Sid off at a friend's house, Ben and Uncle Bert floated into town.

45
00:02:35.714 --> 00:02:40.915
Since Ben didn't have much money to spend, Uncle Bert suggested they go to a thrift shop called

46
00:02:40.955 --> 00:02:42.135
the Thrifty Monster.

47
00:02:47.257 --> 00:02:48.277
place is great!"

48
00:02:48.537 --> 00:02:49.297
Ben exclaimed.

49
00:02:49.317 --> 00:02:53.558
"Look at this old-fashioned vampire cape.

50
00:02:54.159 --> 00:02:55.759
This could work for Mog's costume."

51
00:02:55.779 --> 00:02:58.760
"Did someone say my name?"

52
00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:01.533
Mog's voice echoed from somewhere in the store.

53
00:03:01.553 --> 00:03:07.516
"Huh?" Ben followed the sound of Mog's voice through racks of clothes until he found him.

54
00:03:08.696 --> 00:03:09.857
But Mog wasn't alone.

55
00:03:10.397 --> 00:03:12.598
Jen was with him, and so was Winnie.

56
00:03:12.618 --> 00:03:16.440
"I'm so sorry, Winnie," Ben blurted out.

57
00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:18.040
Winnie nodded.

58
00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:20.601
"You were trying to help," she said.

59
00:03:20.621 --> 00:03:22.142
"It was an accident."

60
00:03:22.162 --> 00:03:23.963
"Hey, can I see that?"

61
00:03:24.403 --> 00:03:26.424
Mog took the vampire cape from Ben.

62
00:03:26.904 --> 00:03:28.965
"This is perfect for my costume!"

63
00:03:30.665 --> 00:03:34.626
Mog swung an imaginary sword through the air as Waldo walked up.

64
00:03:34.646 --> 00:03:36.127
"Hey, everyone.

65
00:03:36.427 --> 00:03:38.907
Look at these in-line skate wheels that I found.

66
00:03:39.608 --> 00:03:43.168
We can put them on the bottom of the cauldron, so we don't have to carry it."

67
00:03:43.188 --> 00:03:45.289
"Great idea!"

68
00:03:45.569 --> 00:03:46.209
Winnie said.

69
00:03:46.229 --> 00:03:47.950
"Look what we found!"

70
00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:50.791
Sonia exclaimed as she and her friends walked up.

71
00:03:52.191 --> 00:03:55.732
"We decided that we like the blue cauldron," Lucy explained.

72
00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.161
"Yeah," Jade nodded.

73
00:03:58.181 --> 00:04:02.985
"But we came to get some cobweb lace and glitter bones to decorate it."

74
00:04:03.005 --> 00:04:05.586
"Wow," Winnie said.

75
00:04:05.606 --> 00:04:06.687
"I think Ms.

76
00:04:06.727 --> 00:04:08.408
Lafang will like that a lot."

77
00:04:08.428 --> 00:04:12.971
"Lafang?" Uncle Bert's eyes grew wide.

78
00:04:12.991 --> 00:04:16.153
"Do you mean Victoria Lafang?"

79
00:04:16.173 --> 00:04:20.096
"Yes, the famous movie star," Mog said.

80
00:04:20.116 --> 00:04:23.058
"She's our director," Ben explained.

81
00:04:23.598 --> 00:04:25.500
Just then something clicked in his mind.

82
00:04:26.476 --> 00:04:28.837
"Hey, she went to Monster Academy.

83
00:04:29.217 --> 00:04:30.838
Was she in your class, Uncle Bert?

84
00:04:31.418 --> 00:04:32.059
Did you know her?"

85
00:04:32.079 --> 00:04:37.641
"Huh?" Uncle Bert quickly adjusted his collar and hurried over to another rack.

86
00:04:39.382 --> 00:04:42.704
"Look at this—it's a nice cloak for one of the guards."

87
00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:49.707
Everyone was laughing as they entered Monster Academy.

88
00:04:51.956 --> 00:04:54.537
At least until they spotted Victoria and Mr.

89
00:04:54.617 --> 00:04:56.457
Freaky outside the auditorium.

90
00:04:56.877 --> 00:04:59.358
Victoria paced nervously as Mr.

91
00:04:59.438 --> 00:05:00.819
Freaky blew his noses.

92
00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.060
have you students been?"

93
00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:08.501
Mr. Freaky said.

94
00:05:08.521 --> 00:05:12.342
"We thought the entire cast and crew quit!"

95
00:05:12.362 --> 00:05:15.203
"Sorry," Jen explained.

96
00:05:15.223 --> 00:05:19.584
"We all met up to get new costumes before rehearsal today."

97
00:05:20.884 --> 00:05:22.886
"We also found a way to save the cauldron!"

98
00:05:23.206 --> 00:05:23.906
Sonia said.

99
00:05:23.926 --> 00:05:28.630
"Actually, it's going to be even better," Jade chimed in.

100
00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:31.992
"What?" Victoria was surprised.

101
00:05:32.012 --> 00:05:33.273
"What do you mean?"

102
00:05:34.014 --> 00:05:39.518
Everyone quickly explained how they'd used all their money to purchase replacement costumes for everyone.

103
00:05:39.538 --> 00:05:44.001
"They're not perfect," Winnie said, "but they'll do."

104
00:05:44.021 --> 00:05:47.824
"Goodness." Victoria looked impressed.

105
00:05:48.372 --> 00:05:51.615
"You're working together like a real theatrical troupe.

106
00:05:52.236 --> 00:05:53.397
I'm proud of you!"

107
00:05:53.417 --> 00:05:57.961
"There's the old Monster Academy spirit."

108
00:05:58.521 --> 00:05:59.802
Mr. Freaky beamed.

109
00:05:59.822 --> 00:06:01.284
"Let's get inside.

110
00:06:01.624 --> 00:06:03.085
I'll help set things up."

111
00:06:03.866 --> 00:06:05.628
The students hurried after Mr.

112
00:06:05.688 --> 00:06:06.949
Freaky and Victoria.

113
00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:11.413
Ben turned to his uncle, who'd been lingering at the back of the crowd.

114
00:06:11.433 --> 00:06:13.375
"Thanks for your help, Uncle Bert.

115
00:06:13.655 --> 00:06:14.736
I'll see you at home later."

116
00:06:15.608 --> 00:06:16.329
"Sure thing."

117
00:06:16.630 --> 00:06:21.318
Uncle Bert turned to float away when Victoria Lafang abruptly spun around.

118
00:06:21.338 --> 00:06:23.281
"Bert?" she said.

119
00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:28.771
that you?"
